# Build output. Both are regenerated by `prepare`, and both are in
# package.json `files` — published from a fresh build, never from the repo.
#
# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and it matters: a bare `client/` matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth, so it also swallowed `src/client/` —
# the entire UI, some 2500 lines, was never committed and `git status` stayed
# clean the whole time. Nothing errors when a source tree is silently ignored.
/lib/
/client/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Test workspace: smoke.mjs renders real films into it with ffmpeg.
/tmp/

node_modules/

# Creative drafts: workspace material, never published.
/drafts/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db